# Batch files need CRLF: cmd.exe mis-parses parenthesised blocks in an
# LF-only file, and this one uses them for the error paths.
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Everything else keeps LF, including the shell script that has to run on
# machines where CRLF would break the shebang.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Kept out of the release bundles `git archive` produces. All of it is build
# or maintenance machinery that nobody downloading a zip has any use for:
# launcher/ is Go source plus 600KB of Windows resource blobs used to stamp
# the icon onto the .exe, and shipping unexplained binaries inside an archive
# named "no-exe" is also how you get another argument with Defender.
launcher/ export-ignore
.github/ export-ignore
.githooks/ export-ignore
scripts/ export-ignore
